    "concluded": true,
    "explanation": "CF-CONFECTIONERY lost 548.5K Units year on year across the four like-for-like branches, moving from 4.4M to 3.9M Units and accounting for 176.5% of the total comparable Units decline. The decline was almost entirely concentrated in one product group, CF-CHOCOLATE, which was down 548.1K Units, and within that especially CHOCOLATE COATED BARS, down 473.5K Units; that one sub-group represents about 86% of the category’s Units loss. By branch, the weakness was broad-based rather than isolated: CFH021 contributed -261.8K Units, CFH018 -155.5K, CFH014 -104.1K, and CFH017 -27.1K. Transactions were also down for the category, from 217.3K to 211.2K, with the largest transaction declines in CFH017 and CFH021, so the Units drop is associated with both fewer transactions and materially fewer Units sold within the chocolate range, especially coated bars. The best next human check is a SKU-level review of CHOCOLATE COATED BARS by branch to see whether the loss is linked to distribution, assortment changes, or stock availability rather than a broad confectionery-wide issue.",
