    "explanation": "CFH021 accounted for SAR 4.18M of comparable Revenue growth, equal to 138.3% of the total like-for-like change, based on the reused baseline rows. A complete CFH021 drill by item category shows the gain was concentrated in a few categories rather than broad-based: CF-MENS FASHION added SAR 805.1K, CF-GROCERY FOOD SAR 580.9K, CF-ELECTRONICS SAR 578.3K, CF-PERSONAL CARE SAR 521.4K, CF-WATCHES & SUNGLASSES SAR 326.8K, and CF-TOYS SAR 306.0K, while some categories such as CF-FRUIT & VEGETABLES were negative in the bundled evidence. This points to CFH021’s growth being likely driven by a mix of stronger Transactions and Units in selected fashion and non-food categories, with the scan’s cited fashion strength consistent with the verified CF-MENS FASHION result and associated fashion gains, rather than a uniform branch-wide uplift. The best next human check is a full CFH021 drill by product_group_name for the fashion categories to confirm whether the branch’s fashion growth is concentrated in a few product groups or spread across the department.",
